    },
    {
      "claim": "Additional benzimidazole or morpholine analogs also show low intrinsic clearance: compound 13 below 12 µL/min/mg (C278), compound 64 below 12 µL/min/mg (C240), and compound 9a at 0.5 ml/min/g liver (C270), so the analog set does not affirmatively indicate high hepatic first-pass extraction.",
      "card_ids": ["C278", "C240", "C270"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "A minority of L6 analogs show higher clearance, such as compound 7d at 135 µL/min/mg (C277), compound 28 at 61 mL/min/kg (C255), and pemigatinib at 25.4 µL/min/mg (C265), but these are less structurally aligned with the query benzimidazole-morpholine-isourea core and do not establish a threshold-relevant outcome for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C277", "C255", "C265"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No L6 record measures the query molecule directly, and the unique N-hydroxycyclopropylamidine isourea moiety is unrepresented in every hepatic stability context, so its metabolic fate remains unknown.",
      "card_ids": ["C249", "C247"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "moderate",
