      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C249", "C247", "C230", "C267", "C253", "C278", "C240", "C270", "C277", "C255", "C265"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement exists.",
    "The unique N-hydroxycyclopropylamidine isourea moiety is absent from all L6 reference molecules, so its hepatic stability is unknown.",
    "No query-specific human first-pass or intravenous comparison data are available.",
    "Solubility, formulation, and dose effects on absorption remain unmeasured for the query.",
    "L6 records are analog measurements with moderate transferability and are not direct bioavailability outcomes."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high is maintained and modestly strengthened. L6 hepatic clearance records for the closest benzimidazole and morpholine analogs are predominantly low to moderate, including KBP-7018, SUVN-G3031, KR-69232, compound 14c, and compound 8, which provides no affirmative evidence of high hepatic first-pass extraction that would drive F below 20%. A few higher-clearance analogs are less structurally aligned with the query core. Confidence remains moderate because all L6 records are analog measurements and the query-specific isourea moiety is unrepresented, but the new evidence reduces rather than increases the presystemic-loss concern."
}

